course: dictionary
lesson: 16166
title: Worthwhile and its meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Worthwhile is an adjective. It describes something that is worth the time, effort or money you spend on it. If something is worthwhile, it is useful or good to do. «The trip to the science museum was worthwhile.» We spent a whole day there and learned lots of new things, so the time was well spent.
explain: The word is made from two parts: worth and while. Worth means good enough to have or do, and while means a period of time. Together they say the time you spend is good enough. «It is worthwhile checking your answers.» Checking takes a few minutes, but it can find mistakes, so those minutes are worth it.
explain: You can also use worthwhile when you talk about money. A deal is worthwhile if what you get is worth more than what you pay. When you meet this word, ask yourself: was the time, effort or money well spent? If yes, the word fits.
fact: Worthwhile is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a trip, a task or a deal.
fact: «Worthwhile» means worth the time, effort or money you spend; useful or good to do.
fact: «A worthwhile trip» is a trip that was good to take.
fact: «It's worthwhile checking your answers» means checking is useful, so it is a good thing to do.
fact: In maths and money, a deal is worthwhile if what you get is worth more than what you pay.
exercise: «We practised our spellings every day, and the test score showed it was worthwhile.» What does worthwhile mean here? | Expensive, costing a lot of money | *Useful, because the effort paid off | Not useful, so we should have stopped | Boring and slow
exercise: Dad says, «Buying the bike was worthwhile, because it has lasted for years.» What does worthwhile show? | The bike was too small | *The bike was good value for the money spent | Dad was sorry he bought it | The bike was broken
exercise: Choose the word that means worth the time and effort. | careless | *worthwhile | wasteful | pointless
test: «Helping Mum tidy the garden took an hour, but it was worthwhile because the flowers could finally grow.» What does worthwhile mean? | Quick and easy | Wasted, because nothing changed | Dirty and messy | *Good to do, because it was worth the time
test: When is a deal worthwhile? | When the shop is closed | *When what you get is worth more than what you pay | When you get nothing at all | When you pay more than the thing is worth
exam: Which sentence uses worthwhile correctly? | *«It is worthwhile practising your times tables each week.» | «I worthwhile my lunch quickly this morning.» | «The rain worthwhile fell all day long.» | «Worthwhile the dog ran into the park.»
